# Documentation

A change is incomplete without docs. Load `.cursor/skills/document-change/SKILL.md` when writing them.

## Where it goes

| Change | Write |
|--------|--------|
| Any proposed commit | `docs/commits/YYYY-MM-DD-<slug>.md` |
| New/changed feature or user story | `docs/features/<name>.md` |
| Layer, entity, persistence, infra, or technology | update `PROJECT_DOCUMENTATION.md` + a focused `docs/` page if the topic is new |
| Agent/process convention | `docs/agent-protocols.md` and `AGENTS.md` |

Do not duplicate novels: commit docs explain **this delta**; feature docs explain **behavior**; `PROJECT_DOCUMENTATION.md` is the system map (keep the “Last updated” date current).

## Commit doc (required)

Use `docs/commits/YYYY-MM-DD-<slug>.md`:

- Why the change exists
- What changed (layers/projects, not a raw file dump)
- Architecture impact (none, or link to the approved question)
- Tests added
- Proposed commit message (same text given to the user)

```text
❌ Chat-only recap, no file under docs/
✅ Commit doc + feature/system doc when behavior or structure changed
```
